---
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
import ResearchCabinet from '../components/ResearchCabinet.astro';
import '../styles/cabinet.css';
export interface Props {}
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Research / Mazze LeCzzare</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Experiments on what models say, how behavior changes, and what the record actually supports. Study-specific instruments and public evidence." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://research.mazzeleczzare.com/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Research / Mazze LeCzzare" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Question. Record. Reconsider. Working instruments for observable model behavior." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://research.mazzeleczzare.com/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-cabinet" preload />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-poster" preload />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-reading" preload />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to research</a>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Mazze LeCzzare Research home">MAZZE LECZZARE<span>RESEARCH</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#instruments">Instruments ↙</a><a href="#evidence">The record ↙</a><a href="#methods">Methods ↙</a><a href="/console.html">Private controls ↗</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <ResearchCabinet />
      <section id="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
        <header class="cabinet-section-head"><h2 id="evidence-title"><span>02</span> The public record</h2><p>Reviewed releases / Source first</p></header>
        <div class="record-intro"><h2>Show your<br/>working.</h2><div><p>The pinned technical smoke releases verify machinery. They are not behavioral findings. Read the citation and source hash here; open the raw record or Rust-generated view when you need the detail.</p><a href="/explorers/index.html">Browse visual evidence ↗</a> · <a href="/prepare.html">Prepare analysis & writing ↗</a></div></div>
        <div id="notification" role="status"></div>
        <div id="releases" class="release-list" aria-live="polite"><p><a href="/api/releases">Read the public release registry ↗</a>. Each record includes its citation and SHA-256 value.</p></div>
        <noscript><p><a href="/api/releases">Public JSON index</a> · <a href="/explorers/index.html">Pinned visual evidence</a>. Loading the live list here requires JavaScript.</p></noscript>
        <p class="record-note">Frozen record ≠ external preregistration · Hash agreement ≠ independent notarization · Missing observations ≠ zero</p>
      </section>
      <div class="context-grid">
        <section class="context-section" id="methods" aria-labelledby="methods-title">
          <header class="cabinet-section-head"><h2 id="methods-title"><span>03</span> Methods, in reach</h2><p>Read before interpreting</p></header>
          <h2>Keep the limits<br/>in the frame.</h2>
          <article class="context-item" id="method-provenance"><span>01</span><div><h3>Provenance before a conclusion</h3><p>A citable release keeps the frozen protocol, raw request/response pairs, exclusions and source hashes together. A hash identifies bytes; it cannot certify an interpretation.</p><a href="/method.html">Full standards & limitations ↗</a></div></article>
          <article class="context-item"><span>02</span><div><h3>Pressure, disclosure & stopping</h3><p>Preserve failures and budget limits. Keep the study's stopping commitments and their implementation limits visible before collecting more observations.</p><a href="/ethics.html">Research ethics ↗</a></div></article>
          <article class="context-item"><span>03</span><div><h3>Interpretation needs another reading</h3><p>Solo ratings are attributed to one reader. Independent human agreement, model assessments and agent contributions are distinct kinds of evidence.</p><a href="/method-audit.html">Selected public method audit ↗</a></div></article>
        </section>
        <section class="context-section" id="connections" aria-labelledby="connections-title">
          <header class="cabinet-section-head"><h2 id="connections-title"><span>04</span> Carry it forward</h2><p>Tools / Archives / Publication</p></header>
          <p class="editorial">A useful record should have<br/>somewhere to go.</p>
          <div class="context-links">
            <article class="context-item"><div><h3>Analysis desk</h3><p>Verify release identity. Prepare a reproducible package, figure or publication brief.</p><a href="/prepare.html">Prepare the work ↗</a></div></article>
            <article class="context-item"><div><h3>Hugging Face</h3><p>A pinned snapshot of two technical smoke releases, with scoped reuse terms.</p><a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/mazzeleczzare/identity-dissolution-evidence/tree/8bdbc469dfab9f3a3795217dde5c69c5ae260b06">Inspect the snapshot ↗</a></div></article>
            <article class="context-item"><div><h3>The press</h3><p>The companion publishing space. Editorial work and evidence releases retain separate review boundaries.</p><a href="https://press.mazzeleczzare.com">Visit the press ↗</a></div></article>
            <article class="context-item"><div><h3>Models & agents</h3><p>Public reading and citation guidance. Reading evidence grants no execution or publication authority.</p><a href="/llms.txt">Read agent guidance ↗</a></div></article>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <footer class="landing-footer"><span>Mazze LeCzzare Frazer / Independent research</span><a href="/api/releases">Public registry ↗</a><a href="/console.html">Owner console ↗</a><a href="#main">Back to the field ↑</a></footer>
    </main>
    <script src="../scripts/cabinet.ts"></script>
    <script src="../scripts/releases.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
